FINAL ANSWER:
Authorship is concentrated. Andrew Gallant holds most of the Rust code that still exists. The next few authors each hold a few percent or less.

I used `git blame -w -M -C` on the Rust files and counted the lines that survive at HEAD. That was 3,710 lines across 9 files, and the numbers below include merging one person's addresses.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Commits (share) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Andrew Gallant | 2,838 | 76.5% | 128 (67.0%) |
| Inès Moreau | 217 | 5.8% | 3 (1.6%) |
| Sebastian Thiel | 74 | 2.0% | 1 (0.5%) |
| Ashley | 68 | 1.8% | 2 (1.0%) |
| Aron Griffis | 59 | 1.6% | 1 (0.5%) |

- **Next in line:** Niv Kaminer (1.2%), mcharsley (1.2%) and Marvin Löbel (1.1%) follow. 31 more authors hold 6.7% together, and the largest of them is Garrett Berg at 0.9%.
- **Bus factor:** it is 1 across all the Rust code counted. That means the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50%. Gallant alone holds 76.5%. Two authors reach 80%.
- **Inès Moreau:** the 5.8% counts three addresses as one person. The tool rates the link as strong, because the name and the GitHub login match across the addresses. It is still a guess from names and addresses, and I did not write a `.mailmap`. Unmerged, she is 120 lines (3.2%) and 97 lines (2.6%) under two separate entries. Either way she is second.
- **Possible duplicate:** Ashley (68 lines) and Ashley Mannix (4 lines) may be the same person. The link is weak, so I kept them separate. Merged they would hold 72 lines (1.9%), which does not change the ranking.
- **Left out:**
  - `src/ucd_tables.rs` (647 lines) is generated and is not in any number.
  - One bot (9 lines, 1 commit) is excluded.
  - No reformat commit was detected automatically.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked 77 commits and set none aside. I inspected one candidate, `c584a1d` "style: switch to rustfmt" by Gallant. It touched 9 files with 243 insertions and 260 deletions. I re-ran without it. Gallant drops to 2,830 lines (76.3%), Aron Griffis rises to 63 lines (1.7%), and the other rows barely change. I kept it in the table above, and the conclusion holds either way.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use `-w -M -C`, which moved 151 lines in 3 files to other authors. Without copy detection, Gallant has 2,989 lines (80.6%), Garrett Berg has 0 and Niv Kaminer has 15 (0.4%, against 1.2% with it).
- **Same address, several names:** Niv Kaminer also appears as `nivkner`, and Alisha also appears as Alisha Aneja. Each pair shares one address and is counted as one person.

These numbers show whose lines survive. They say nothing about code quality, review work or design work.
